        "title": "Kiwi Buddha",
        "alternate_title": [],
        "description": "Kiwi Buddha follows the journey of seven-year-old Rinpoche as he becomes the first Buddhist High Lama incarnated in the Southern Hemisphere. ‘Venerable Pong Re Sung Rap Tulku Rinpoche' is a schoolboy from Kaukapakapa, just north of Auckland. The film documents Rinpoche's journey as he leaves small-town New Zealand behind (along with McDonald's and Pokémon) to travel to a grand Himalayan monastery where he will spend his next 20 years studying Buddhism. Kiwi Buddha sold to the National Geographic channel and to 60 territories. The backgrounder article offers a peek at the making of the film.",
